  "notes": "'In this design the rooms are all on one level as they will occasionally be preferred by many.' The minimum the book argues for a labouring family - a living room, a scullery and three bedrooms, one for the parents, one for the boys, one for the girls - with the loft and the cistern in the roof. A mirrored pair, one half transcribed. The plate prints dimensions but the scan of it is a coarse halftone and they cannot be read with confidence, so none are recorded. Gothic, stone preferable; 250 pounds the pair.",
